body:
Just so I'm clear, you're asking if browsers "prepare a script" when the `src` element is _removed_, right? From testing out the following snippet:

```js
const script = document.createElement('script');
// Invalid, so the script won't execute upon insertion.
script.type = 'foo';
script.src = 'https://google.com';
script.innerText = 'console.log("static text");'
document.body.append(script);

// Make script valid again, but don't immediately execute it.
script.type = 'module';
// See if this kicks off execution
script.removeAttribute('src');
<no execution>
```

...removing the src attribute does not trigger script preparation in any browser. I'll write a test case for this, but please verify that this is what you had in mind with this comment.
